  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.ApproachHakon": "You approach Hakon the Salamander. He strains against his bonds, yelling at you to get Hel and get out before it's too late. You roll your eyes and carry on."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.ApproachSalamander": "You approach the Salamander strapped to the table. He looks at you with his one good eye, warily gauging you as you approach."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.HeliaSentMe": "[pg]You shake your head and tell him that it was Helia who sent you."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.HereToRescueYou": "[pg]You tell him that you're here to rescue him as it happens."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.MyLittleHel": "[pg][say: H... Helia? My little Hel?] he asks in disbelief. With a slight grin, you tell him that 'little' Hel isn't so little anymore. He laughs, but for an instant you think he might be about to cry. [say: Of... of course she is. My little girl's all grown up. Oh, what I wouldn't give to meet her...]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.NotComplaining": "[pg][say: What!?] he says, wide-eyed. [say: Hey, I'm not complaining, mind you, but pardon me for being surprised. I've been locked up in this shithole for... Marae, must have been fifteen, twenty years now. Why now? Who sent you? My wife?]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.NotFarAway": "[pg]You tell him that she's not far away at all... just a few floors up, in fact."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.SightForSoreEyes": "[pg][say: Well, aren't you a sight for sore eyes,] he laughs, his voice little more than a rasp. [say: About time somebody put a boot up that punk bitch's ass. Ha! Hey, the name's Hakon. I'd shake your hand, but, uh, I'm a bit tied up at the moment as it were. So, what brings an outsider all the way up here?]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.SmileApproachHakon": "You smile as you approach Hakon the Salamander. He starts to yell at you again, but you snap at him to hush. You explain that Hel and Kiri are waiting outside and that the broodmother has been defeated. Both sets of keys jingling in your hands. He watches you approach silently, his eyes wary but hopeful. You quickly undo his bonds, freeing him for the first time in years. He struggles to sit, but nearly collapses. You catch him before he hurts himself and, throwing his arm over your shoulder, help the old salamander toward the stairs..."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HelDungeonPrisonerTalk.YouBroughtHerHere": "[pg][say: WHAT!?] he yells, straining against the chains that bind him. [say: You brought Hel here!? What were you thinking? Go and get her out of here. NOW!]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.AskAFavor": "[pg][say: Actually, champ, I wanted to... um, well... ask a favor, I guess.] Hel says awkwardly, suddenly avoiding eye contact. [say: I wouldn't ask if it wasn't important, or something I could do on my own, or... Ah, shit.] From inside her cloak, Hel produces a dirty, dented flask and takes a long swig of what smells like pure grain alcohol. While she drinks, you urge her to tell you what's on her mind."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.AskIfThatsTrue": " You ask her if that's true. With a little wink, she answers, [say: Well, it's not entirely untrue...]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.AskWhyPiqued": "[pg]You ask her why that's piqued her interest so much; she lives some ways away from the mountains after all."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.BeforeBeddingDown": "Before bedding down for the night, you make one last check of your camp's perimeter, making sure all your traps and defenses are still in place and primed in the event of a surprise nighttime assault. As you come to the outermost parts of your makeshift camp, you notice a cloaked stranger approaching out of the evening darkness. You're about to ready your [weapon], but you recognize the shapely figure of Hel the salamander walking towards you, hips a-sway underneath her loose traveling cloak."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.BelchesThunderously": "[pg]She belches thunderously, shakes it off, and sighs. [say: It's like this, Champ: a little birdie told me that there's this tremendous roost of harpies up in the high mountains, dozens of the bitches all packed together. That's bad enough, right? But now, some of them have been showing up with red scales all over their arms and legs... and fire on their tails.]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.DoYouAgreeQuestion": "[pg]Do you agree to help Helia? She'd probably be <b>very</b> grateful..."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.FeatherBitches": "[pg][say: Normally I wouldn't give two shits about what a bunch of feather-bitches are doing. But scales and fire? Sound like someone you know?] Before you can answer, you feel Hel's warm tail curl around your shoulders, hugging you right up against her. She takes another long swig from her flask. It's starting to smell like someone lit a brewery on fire next to you. [say: What I'm saying is that there's a chance that there's a poor, abused salamander tied up in this roost of theirs, being used as breeding stock for years and years now, fathering a whole new generation of harpies. Even if you don't give a shit about the birds, it would... mean a lot to me if you'd help me break him out. Look, [name], I'm a mean bitch in a fight - you know that - but even I can't take on a whole roost of harpies solo. And, well, you're the only person I trust one-hundred percent. To have my back, you know?]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.GetRestOfInfo": "[pg]You spend the next few minutes getting the rest of her information out in the open - they live in an old abandoned watchtower, she says, and number perhaps two dozen. As she talks, you note a desperate tone in Hel's voice, and more than once she repeats that she can't do it by herself, or trust anyone but you to help."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.GuideHerToCamp": ", and guide her over to the camp proper."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.HandOnYourThigh": " Her hand slides over to rest on your thigh."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.LazilyPointOutTraps": "lazily point out your traps to the not-quite-intruder"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.RushOverStopHel": "quickly rush over and stop Hel before she loses a leg to one of your traps"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.SalamanderCalls": "[pg][say: Hey there, [name]!] the salamander calls, handily picking her way through your maze of traps. She gives you a quick embrace and, taking your hand in hers, leads you back to the camp proper."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.SalamanderShouts": "[pg][say: [name]!] the salamander shouts, waving emphatically as she approaches. [say: Shit, do you have any idea how hard you are to track down? I've been looking for you everywhere!] You "
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.SheStrokesYourFlank": " [say: She gives your flank a slow, affectionate stroke.]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaDiscovery.SitHerDown": "[pg]You sit the salamander down near your campfire and ask her what brought her all the way from the plains to your humble abode. She shrugs lightly and says, [say: Maybe I just wanted some company tonight.]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaHakonTalk.AssureItsTrue": "[pg]You assure her that it's true. The salamander she came here to rescue is none other than father, Hakon."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaHakonTalk.DontBelieveIt": "[pg][say: I don't believe it,] Hel says, rubbing at the corners of her eyes. [say: I thought all these years... I was sure he was dead. How... No. It doesn't matter,] she says, turning to the broodmother beneath her."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaHakonTalk.PayForWhatDid": " [say: You're going to pay for what you did to my father, you bitch. I promise you that.]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaHakonTalk.TellHelWhosDownstairs": "You decide to tell Hel who, exactly, is chained up downstairs. When you do, she simply stares at you, wide-eyed."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaHakonTalk.ThatCantBe": "[pg][say: Wha... what. No, that's not... It can't be...]"
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaKiriTalk.AskAboutKiri": "You ask Hel about the half-breed girl that helped the two of you find this place, and offered you information below."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaKiriTalk.AskMoreThanFriends": "[pg]With a knowing look, you ask if they're more than just friends."
  "Scenes.Heldungeon.HeliaKiriTalk.BoppedTheBull": "[pg][say: So, I bopped the bull on the head and saved her. More to keep down the 'taur population than actually help her, but hey. She certainly appreciated it. Been friends ever since.]"
